msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# colors"
msgstr "# colors"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."
msgstr "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only fargeberegning som speiler InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhjelpere (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex values. pantoken emits\n`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through `light-dark()`), so the\nmath has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string built from\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) and\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nboth Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the token even when it's a\nscheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-code a derived shade."
msgstr "InstUI beregner disse ved byggetid med `tinycolor2` mot konkrete hex-verdier. pantoken emitterer\n`var(--instui-*)`-referanser som løses i nettleseren (ofte gjennom `light-dark()`), så\nberegningen må skje i CSS i stedet. Hver hjelper returnerer en CSS-fargestreng bygget fra\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) og\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nbegge er grunnleggende moderne nettleserfunksjoner — slik at ett enkelt uttrykk følger tokenet selv når det er et\nskjema-avhengig `light-dark()`-par. Bruk dem der du ellers ville hardkodet en avledet nyanse."

